<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92511" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥίον</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ], τό</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>any jutting part</i> of a mountain, whether upwards
			or forwards; hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>peak</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ ῥίον Οὐλύμποιο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					8.25
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				14.154
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				225
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥ. ὀρέων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					9.191
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥ. οὔρεος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Ap.</u>
					139
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>headland</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				3.295
			</span></i>; hence as pr. name of several places, esp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ῥ. Μολυκρικόν</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ῥ. Ἀχαϊκόν</span> at the mouth of the gulf
			of Corinth, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.86
			</span></i> (cf. <i><span class="en">
				84
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> later,
				<i>bay formed by a foreland</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				15.3
			</span></i>. (Perh. akin to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥίς</span>, cf.
				<i>Ness, Naze</i> with <i>nose.</i>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
